            c.register(Notifier.class, "push", true, Scope.SINGLETON, x -> new Email("push"));
            c.register(Notifier.class, "fax", true, Scope.SINGLETON, x -> new Email("fax"));
            ok(raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> c.get(Notifier.class)).getMessage().contains("found 4"), "two primaries must fail too");
        });
        test("factories resolve their dependencies", () -> {
            var c = new Container();
            c.register(Clock.class, "clock", false, Scope.SINGLETON, x -> new Clock());
            c.register(Notifier.class, "email", false, Scope.SINGLETON, x -> new Email("email"));
            c.register(Service.class, "service", false, Scope.SINGLETON, x -> new Service(x.get(Notifier.class), x.get(Clock.class)));
            ok(c.get(Service.class).clock() == c.get(Clock.class), "the service got the shared clock");
        });
        test("a singleton is created on first use, once", () -> {
            var c = new Container();
            int[] made = {0};
            c.register(Clock.class, "clock", false, Scope.SINGLETON, x -> { made[0]++; return new Clock(); });
            eq(made[0], 0);
            c.get(Clock.class);
            c.get(Clock.class);
            eq(made[0], 1);
        });
        test("a missing bean fails clearly (boundary)", () -> ok(raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> new Container().get(Clock.class)).getMessage().contains("no bean"), "message should say no bean"));
        test("getAll of an unknown type is empty", () -> ok(new Container().getAll(Notifier.class).isEmpty(), "expected empty"));
        System.exit(report());
    }
    // ─── end tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
}

fund-java/17-spring-ioc-and-dependency-i.explanation:
Without the PROTOTYPE branch, `instance` caches every bean on first use, so a prototype is shared like a singleton and two `get` calls return the same object. The starter fails only "singletons are shared, prototypes are new", on its `prototype must be new` check. Every other test uses singletons only, or no beans at all, so caching everything passes them. Restore the branch, so the factory runs each time for a prototype and the cache serves singletons only:

```java
private Object instance(Reg r) {
    if (r.scope == Scope.PROTOTYPE) return r.factory.apply(this);
    if (r.instance == null) r.instance = r.factory.apply(this);
    return r.instance;
}
```

Dropping the `null` check instead, so the factory runs on every call, is not a fix: singletons stop being shared, and "singletons are shared, prototypes are new", "factories resolve their dependencies" and "a singleton is created on first use, once" fail.
